  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Leadership Exchange Program 4.0 (YLEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While YLEP 4.0 builds on the learnings gained from the three previous exchanges, it also introduces significant new elements. A key change in this iteration is the relocation of YLs from Nairobi to Mombasa. This shift places greater responsibility on KRCS, which will now play an even larger role in supporting the YLs, given the increased distance from DRC&apos;s direct involvement. The YLs will contribute to two major projects. The first, CISU project, provides them with the opportunity to engage with youth and support the implementation of income-generating activities within their communities. The second, UCRB, offers experience in evaluating a large-scale development project, utilizing and enhancing their technical skills.</narrative>
  </description>
